# How to cite the rcsd.info data. GitHub's "Cite this repository" button and
# Zenodo both read this file.
#
# `license` names the data license only. CFF reads a list of licenses as
# "either one", so adding MIT here would offer the data under MIT. The code's
# MIT license is in LICENSE; README.md states the split.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this data, please cite it as below and include the date you
  retrieved it: the data is updated continuously and has no numbered releases.
type: dataset
title: "rcsd.info: Open Data for Redwood City School District"
abstract: >-
  Independently compiled public records for the Redwood City School District,
  a TK-8 public school district in Redwood City, California: board meetings,
  agendas, attachments and recordings with transcripts, board policies, school
  profiles and accountability reports, state education data, budgets, vendor
  payments, calendars and committees, in English and Spanish. Not an official
  district product. AI-generated summaries, translations and transcripts are
  labeled as such and are not official records. The CC BY 4.0 license covers
  this compilation, not the underlying district, county and state records.
authors:
  - family-names: Weekly
    given-names: David E.
    website: "https://david.weekly.org"
url: "https://rcsd.info"
repository-code: "https://github.com/dweekly/rcsd-meetings"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - open data
  - civic data
  - public records
  - school district
  - school board
  - K-8 education
  - Redwood City
  - California
